  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Core recurring-revenue momentum is solid, driven by product investments, but persistent weakness in the professional services segment is dragging on organic growth and triggered a modest full-year revenue guidance reduction. The uneven performance has split analyst views — several bullish calls are offset by a prominent sell rating and recent price-target cuts, leaving sentiment cautious and the outlook uncertain.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is doubling down on the shift to recurring revenue as the primary long-term indicator of business quality. Management proactively trimmed guidance to acknowledge services headwinds, demonstrating transparency but tempering near‑term expectations. Insider ownership remains high, yet the chief revenue officer’s recent share sale adds a subtle note of caution, balancing confidence in the strategy with near‑term prudence.",
